  "street_name": "THISTLEWAITE ROAD",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-371c92be-7fff-a104-b2b0-9a93f6933950&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;The proposed &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;removal of existing front boundary treatment and installation of an integrated cycle and refuse store, by reason of its inappropriate height, scale and materiality, would comprise an incongruous, discordant and overly prominent feature, to the detriment of the character and appearance of the site and wider streetscape, contrary to London Plan policy D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach), Hackney’s LP33 policy LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) and Hackney’s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
